Online Food Ordering System

A console-based Online Food Ordering System developed in C++ for a B.Tech CSE Project-Based Learning (PBL) project.

Features

* User registration and login
* Arithmetic CAPTCHA verification
* Display registered users
* Food menu with prices and categories
* Add items to a shopping cart
* View cart and calculate the subtotal
* Sort the food menu by price
* Home delivery and self-pickup options
* Automatic bill calculation and order confirmation

Technologies Used

* C++
* Structures and functions
* Vectors and arrays
* Input validation
* Modular programming
* Git and GitHub

Project Structure

* main.cpp — Main program and navigation menu
* models.h — Shared data structures and declarations
* common.cpp — Common input and utility functions
* captcha.cpp — CAPTCHA verification
* users.cpp — User registration, login, and registered users
* menu.cpp — Food menu and price sorting
* cart.cpp — Shopping cart operations
* delivery.cpp — Home delivery and self-pickup
* checkout.cpp — Bill calculation and order confirmation

How to Compile and Run

Make sure a C++ compiler such as GCC is installed.

Compile all source files together:

g++ main.cpp common.cpp captcha.cpp users.cpp menu.cpp cart.cpp delivery.cpp checkout.cpp -o food_ordering

Run on Windows:

.\food_ordering.exe

Run on Linux:

./food_ordering

How to Use

1. Register a user.
2. Log in using the registered User ID.
3. Browse the food menu.
4. Add food items to the cart.
5. Select home delivery or self-pickup.
6. Review the bill and confirm the order.

Project Purpose

This project demonstrates modular C++ programming, data structures, user input handling, and a basic food ordering workflow.

